//! FIXTURE: refused form `nested_command_declaration`.
//! EXPECT: refuse command_declaration_nested
//! PROVENANCE: AUTHORED.
//! ABSENT FROM SUITE: Just has no declaration nesting to carry a specimen of.
//!   The form exists only because AWL has two declaration layers — the
//!   command half a gate leg consumes, and the assembly half it cannot reach
//!   — and this is amendment 1's CONVERSE fence.
//! WHY REFUSED: a command is declared at the TOP LEVEL and referenced by a
//!   step. Nesting one inside a recipe would put a gate-leg declaration where
//!   no reader of the top level meets it, which would make the recipe layer
//!   reachable from a gate leg by a second route.

workflow just_nested_command_declaration
  outcome done: type String, route success

recipe stage
  command inner
    program "echo"
    admits "--"
  step run_it
    runs command inner

step go
  route done("ok")
